course: dictionary
lesson: 15732
title: Transient: here for a short time
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Transient means lasting only a short time. Something transient passes quickly, like a rainbow or a sudden shower. «The sunshine was transient, and the clouds were back within ten minutes.» The clues are «within ten minutes», so transient must mean short-lived.
explain: Look for clue words that show time. Words like «only», «for a moment», «soon» and «within minutes» often point to a transient thing. «The flash of light was transient, gone in less than a second.» Ask yourself: does this thing last, or does it pass quickly?
explain: Transient can also describe a person. A transient is someone who stays in one place for a short time before moving on. «Many transients stayed in the town for only a few weeks.» In that sentence, the people are not staying for long, and that is the meaning of transient.
fact: Transient means lasting only a short time.
fact: A transient pain is one that does not last, and it goes away soon.
fact: As a noun, a transient is a person who moves from place to place, often without a permanent home. This use is mostly found in the United States.
fact: «Transient» is the opposite of «permanent», which means lasting for a very long time.
fact: Scientists use transient for changes that happen quickly and then stop, such as a short flash of light or a brief spike in a reading.
exercise: «The sunshine was transient, and the clouds were back within ten minutes.» What does transient mean here? | Bright and warm all day | Very large | Easy to see | *Lasting only a short time
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to transient? | Ancient | Permanent | *Brief | Heavy
exercise: «A transient person stays in a place only for a short time before moving on.» What is a transient person? | A teacher at a school | Someone who never leaves home | A very old person | *Someone who stays in a place only for a short time
test: «The doctor said the pain was transient and would soon pass.» What does transient mean? | Lasting forever | Very sharp | *Lasting only a short time | Hidden from view
test: «A child's anger was transient, and soon she was laughing again.» What does transient show about the anger? | It lasted for years | It was hard to see | *It passed quickly | It was very large
exam: «The flash of light in the science lab was transient, gone in less than a second.» Which meaning fits best? | Lasting for ever | Dangerous to touch | Bright and colourful | *Passing quickly
